  "conclusions_for_comparison": [
    "A global low-width grid can strongly bias weak weights or round them to zero; floating range and integer linear resolution have different tradeoffs.",
    "The quantization step of one edge does not equal the achievable resolution of a collective row gain. Actual contextual responses, not only row sums, determine adequacy.",
    "Training precision costs must be counted. A full-precision value per edge is much more expensive than per-neuron state; no master-weight copy or optimizer state is presumed.",
    "A scale attached to a row is mathematically compatible with incoming gather, but choosing one requires actual range/error evidence and preserves training ownership of weight policy."
